en they had heard these words, they marvelled, and left him, and went their way.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and asked him,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒsaying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife, deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:likewise the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ$And last of all the woman died also.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYTherefore in the resurrection whose wife shall she be of the seven? for they all had her.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Jesus answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnFor in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmBut as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken unto you by God, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwI am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd when the multitude heard this, they were astonished at his doctrine.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book'§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse$¦verses“„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgBut when the Pharisees had heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, they were gathered together.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUThen one of them, which was a lawyer, asked him a question, tempting him, and saying,¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ2Master, which is the great commandment in the law?¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book'§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse(¦verses”„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwJesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ(This is the first and great commandment.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIAnd the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book'§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse.¦verses–„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them,¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVsaying, What think ye of Christ? whose son is he? They say unto him, The son of David.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHHe saith unto them, How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text»The LORD said unto my Lord,¦layout ‚¤textºSit thou on my right hand,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ(Till I make thine enemies thy footstool?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ/If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd no man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask him any more questions.¦layout ªlast_verse.